## Why This Is Asked
Tests for idempotent POST semantics are common in production APIs to avoid duplicate side effects. This question assesses practical planning, edge-case coverage, and tooling familiarity.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent POST with Idempotency-Key usage
- Database state validation vs. idempotent responses
- Rate limiting and retry behavior
- Schema validation and header propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test idea (pseudo):
const payload = { itemId: 'A1', qty: 1, customerId: 'C42' };
const key = 'idemp-123';
const r1 = post('/orders', payload, {'X-Idempotency-Key': key});
const r2 = post('/orders', payload, {'X-Idempotency-Key': key});
assert(r1.orderId === r2.orderId);
assert(r1.status in [201,200]);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency across multiple services (shipping, billing) sharing the same key?
- How would you simulate and verify backoff correctness under sustained 429 responses?

